---
// The advanced end of the practice, and the natural next question for any
// client who actually adopts what we build. Nobody in the competitive set is
// having this conversation.
//
// SOURCING NOTE (internal): posted as a conversation we have, not a
// productized offering — the copy promises judgment and arithmetic, both of
// which we can deliver today. It does not promise a deliverable that would
// have to be invented on the spot. The live worked example (per-seat licence
// cost against hardware, with servers freeing up during a platform migration)
// stays internal. Economics refreshed monthly.
//
// One thing this block must never say, in any form: "we will save you money
// on AI." The honest framing is that we tell you when to switch and when not
// to, and most of the time the answer is not yet.
const paras = [
  'Most companies are fine paying per token. Some are not, and the crossover arrives faster than people expect once a tool gets real adoption across a workforce. We have watched clients go from a few hundred dollars a month to a number that makes the CFO ask questions, without anyone deciding to spend more.',
  'There is a point where owning the hardware and running open models beats renting the API, and there is a point well before that where it is a distraction. We will tell you which side of it you are on, with the arithmetic attached. Usually the answer is a split: your own model handling the routine internal volume, commercial models where the quality genuinely matters.',
  'We run this analysis for our own business first. You are getting a recommendation we have already had to live with.',
];
---

<section id="self-hosting" class="hosting section section-narrow surface-tint">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="section-label">The conversation nobody else is having</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">When renting the models stops making sense.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="hosting-prose reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 90ms">
      {paras.map(p => <p class="hosting-para">{p}</p>)}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .hosting-prose {
    transition-delay: var(--reveal-delay, 0ms);
  }

  .hosting-para {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.78;
    color: var(--charcoal);
  }

  .hosting-para + .hosting-para {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }

  /* The last line is the credibility move — it gets the rule. */
  .hosting-para:last-child {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--terracotta);
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
  }
</style>
